                    Websites
                  </th>
                  <td class="py-2 text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 space-y-0.5 align-top">
                    <div>
                      <a href="https://www.rajnikantg.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="hover:underline">
                        rajnikantg.in ↗
                      </a>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                      <a href="https://www.prometrion.com" class="hover:underline">
                        prometrion.com
                      </a>
                    </div>
                  </td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </aside>

          <!-- ==========================================
               LEAD INTRODUCTORY PARAGRAPHS
               ========================================== -->
          <div class="space-y-4 text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed text-neutral-800 dark:text-neutral-200 font-sans mb-8">
            
            <!-- Platform Lead: November 2025 Side Project Genesis & Single-Handed Authorship -->
            <p class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 font-normal">
              <strong>Prometrion</strong> is an independent software company, technology platform, and digital solutions ecosystem dedicated to engineering high-performance digital products, automation systems, applied artificial intelligence software, and modern web applications. Established in <strong>November 2025 as a side project</strong> by software engineer <strong>Rajnikant Gaurav</strong>, the initiative rapidly developed from an exploratory engineering sandbox into Gaurav's <strong>ultimate company</strong> and primary corporate vehicle. Crucially, Rajnikant Gaurav has built Prometrion <strong>fully on his own</strong> as a solo builder and chief architect—originating the system design, developing full-stack source code, integrating cloud edge runtimes, and engineering its complete digital product catalog without external engineering dependencies.
            </p>

            <!-- Founder Biographical Lead -->
            <p>
              <strong>Rajnikant Gaurav</strong> (born 20 September 2005) is an independent software developer, technology enthusiast, AI explorer, open-source contributor, and entrepreneur from Uttar Pradesh, India. His career and development philosophy are centered on one primary principle: <em>learn technology, build with it, and turn ideas into real products.</em>
            </p>

            <p>
              Born in Dadar, Ballia, Uttar Pradesh, Gaurav demonstrated an early curiosity toward computing and software systems. This interest matured into a structured pursuit of computer science, full-stack engineering, practical artificial intelligence applications, and startup entrepreneurship.
            </p>

            <p>
              He is currently active as an independent engineer and the founder of Prometrion, a software company dedicated to engineering digital products, automation systems, and applied artificial intelligence software. His portfolio and technical developments are documented at his personal domain, <a href="https://www.rajnikantg.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 font-medium hover:underline">www.rajnikantg.in</a>.
            </p>
          </div>

        <!-- ==========================================
             SECTION 1: EARLY LIFE AND COMPUTER SCIENCE
             ========================================== -->
        <section id="early-life" class="scroll-mt-24 mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif sm:font-sans font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white border-b border-neutral-200 dark:border-white/10 pb-2 flex items-center justify-between overflow-hidden">
            <span class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-sm font-mono text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400">01.</span>
              <span>Early life and computer science</span>
            </span>
            <span class="text-xs font-mono font-normal text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 hover:underline cursor-pointer select-none">[edit]</span>
          </h2>

          <div class="mt-4 space-y-3.5 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 font-sans">
            <p>
              Rajnikant Gaurav pursued a Bachelor of Technology in Computer Science and Engineering, during which his initial curiosity toward programming evolved into a broader discipline of software engineering.
            </p>
            <p>
              Rather than treating computer science solely as an academic curriculum, Gaurav approached it as an avenue to master digital architectures and build software autonomously. Throughout his engineering studies, he gained practical proficiency across modern stacks including:
            </p>

            <!-- Luminous Stack Capsule -->
            <div class="my-4 p-4 bg-neutral-50 dark:bg-[#121216] border border-neutral-200 dark:border-white/10 text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono text-neutral-800 dark:text-neutral-200 rounded-lg shadow-whisper overflow-hidden">
              <div class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-neutral-400 dark:text-neutral-500 font-semibold mb-2">Technical Toolchain & Environments</div>
              <p class="leading-relaxed text-cyan-700 dark:text-cyan-300">
                JavaScript • React • Node.js • Express.js • Python • PostgreSQL • Tailwind CSS • Git • REST APIs • Relational Databases • Modern Cloud Deployment
              </p>
            </div>

            <p>
              He quickly shifted from passive study to active project execution, creating web applications, full-stack backends, experimental AI implementations, developer tooling, and business concepts with market viability. This transition—from absorbing technology to manufacturing solutions with it—formed the foundational core of his career.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- ==========================================
             SECTION 2: INDEPENDENT DEVELOPER AND BUILDER MINDSET
             ========================================== -->
        <section id="builder-mindset" class="scroll-mt-24 mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif sm:font-sans font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white border-b border-neutral-200 dark:border-white/10 pb-2 flex items-center justify-between overflow-hidden">
            <span class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-sm font-mono text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400">02.</span>
              <span>Independent developer and builder mindset</span>
            </span>
            <span class="text-xs font-mono font-normal text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 hover:underline cursor-pointer select-none">[edit]</span>
          </h2>

          <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 font-sans">
            <p>
              Gaurav distinguishes between the conventional definition of a programmer and that of an independent builder. While a developer writes software to specification, a builder analyzes the problem holistically by evaluating six fundamental operational questions:
            </p>

            <!-- 6 Questions Bento Grid -->
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-3 my-4 overflow-hidden">
              <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-neutral-50/80 dark:bg-white/[0.03] border border-neutral-200 dark:border-white/10 shadow-whisper">
                <span class="text-xs font-mono text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 font-bold block mb-1">01. THE PROBLEM</span>
                <p class="font-medium text-neutral-900 dark:text-white text-sm">What problem am I solving?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-neutral-50/80 dark:bg-white/[0.03] border border-neutral-200 dark:border-white/10 shadow-whisper">
                <span class="text-xs font-mono text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 font-bold block mb-1">02. AUDIENCE</span>
                <p class="font-medium text-neutral-900 dark:text-white text-sm">Who needs the solution?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-neutral-50/80 dark:bg-white/[0.03] border border-neutral-200 dark:border-white/10 shadow-whisper">
                <span class="text-xs font-mono text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 font-bold block mb-1">03. FUNCTIONALITY</span>
                <p class="font-medium text-neutral-900 dark:text-white text-sm">How should the product work?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-neutral-50/80 dark:bg-white/[0.03] border border-neutral-200 dark:border-white/10 shadow-whisper">
                <span class="text-xs font-mono text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 font-bold block mb-1">04. ERGONOMICS</span>
                <p class="font-medium text-neutral-900 dark:text-white text-sm">How should it be designed?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-neutral-50/80 dark:bg-white/[0.03] border border-neutral-200 dark:border-white/10 shadow-whisper">
                <span class="text-xs font-mono text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 font-bold block mb-1">05. SCALABILITY</span>
                <p class="font-medium text-neutral-900 dark:text-white text-sm">How will the technology scale?</p>
